      "id": 1,
      "text": "St. Clement was founded in 1870 by a colony of German Catholics and named after Saint Clement of Rome.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Clement%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office operated in St. Clement from 1870 until 1882, marking the town’s early communication hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Clement%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The parish was officially established on August 11, 1871, when ten acres were deeded to Archbishop Peter Kenrick.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://stclementmo.org/our-parish/parish-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first brick church, seating 70, was completed in 1873 at a cost of $2,000 and became the community’s spiritual center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://stclementmo.org/our-parish/parish-history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A new Gothic‑style church began construction on August 18, 1897, and was dedicated on May 11, 1898, replacing the original building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://stclementmo.org/our-parish/parish-history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The present St. Clement church held its first Mass in June 1969 and was dedicated on October 19, 1969.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
